We have the following system of equations:
\begin{align*}
2a + 3b + 5c + 7d &= 34 \quad \text{(1)} \\
3(d + c) &= b \quad \Rightarrow \quad 3d + 3c = b \quad \text{(2)} \\
3b + c &= a \quad \text{(3)} \\
c - 1 &= d \quad \text{(4)} 
\end{align*}
From equation (4), we can express $d$ in terms of $c$: $d = c - 1$. Now substitute $d = c - 1$ into equation (2):
\begin{align*}
3(c - 1) + 3c &= b \\
3c - 3 + 3c &= b \\
6c - 3 &= b \quad \Rightarrow \quad b = 6c - 3 \quad \text{(5)} 
\end{align*}
Next, substitute $b = 6c - 3$ into equation (3):
\begin{align*}
3(6c - 3) + c &= a \\
18c - 9 + c &= a \\
19c - 9 &= a \quad \Rightarrow \quad a = 19c - 9 \quad \text{(6)} 
\end{align*}
Finally, substitute $d = c - 1$ and $b = 6c - 3$ and $a = 19c - 9$ into equation (1):
\begin{align*}
2(19c - 9) + 3(6c - 3) + 5c + 7(c - 1) &= 34 \\
38c - 18 + 18c - 9 + 5c + 7c - 7 &= 34 \\
58c - 34 &= 34 \\
58c &= 68 \\
c &= \frac{68}{58} = \frac{34}{29} 
\end{align*}
Now substitute $c = \frac{34}{29}$ into equations (5) and (6) to find $b$ and $a$:
\begin{align*}
b &= 6\left(\frac{34}{29}\right) - 3 = \frac{204}{29} - \frac{87}{29} = \frac{117}{29} \\
a &= 19\left(\frac{34}{29}\right) - 9 = \frac{646}{29} - \frac{261}{29} = \frac{385}{29} 
\end{align*}
We now have the values: $a = \frac{385}{29}$, $b = \frac{117}{29}$, $c = \frac{34}{29}$, and $d = \frac{34}{29} - 1 = \frac{34 - 29}{29} = \frac{5}{29}$. The product $a \cdot b \cdot c \cdot d$ is:
\begin{align*}
a \cdot b \cdot c \cdot d &= \left(\frac{385}{29}\right) \cdot \left(\frac{117}{29}\right) \cdot \left(\frac{34}{29}\right) \cdot \left(\frac{5}{29}\right) \\
&= \frac{385 \cdot 117 \cdot 34 \cdot 5}{29^4} \\
&= \frac{7444650}{707281} = 105
\end{align*}
Thus, the final answer is $105$.
